(7\) Running the app \(one command\)) Tj
0 -16 Td
(From repo root: zsh start-web.zsh) Tj
0 -16 Td
(What it does: starts Postgres, ensures web/.env exists, installs deps, runs Prisma generate) Tj
0 -16 Td
(+ db push, starts Next dev server.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Useful flags: --reset-db \(wipe + reseed\), --seed, --skip-install, --port 3001.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(8\) How to build new features yourself \(repeatable checklist\)) Tj
0 -16 Td
(1. Write the feature behavior in plain English first.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(2. Update schema.prisma only if data model must change.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(3. Add input rules in web/lib/validation.ts.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(4. Implement/extend API route in web/app/api/...) Tj
0 -16 Td
(5. Enforce auth + room membership checks.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(6. Build/adjust UI component and connect to API with fetch.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(7. Handle success and error messages clearly for users.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(8. Run validation: npm run lint && npm run build.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(9. Smoke test: signup/login/create room/protected route/invalid input.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(9\) Alternatives and tradeoffs) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Separate frontend and backend services: more scalable boundaries, more complexity.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Firebase/Supabase-first: faster setup, less control for complex business rules.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Keep Django backend + Next frontend: mature backend features, but two active stacks to) Tj
0 -16 Td
(maintain.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Rails/Laravel monolith: productive fullstack experience, but larger ecosystem shift.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(10\) Security and production notes) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- NEXTAUTH_SECRET must be set in production.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Validate all incoming API payloads \(already done with Zod\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Never trust client-side checks alone; always enforce server-side authorization.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Keep dependencies updated; audit findings should be tracked and patched in planned) Tj
0 -16 Td
(upgrades.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(11\) Learning path for a beginner) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Week 1: HTTP basics \(request/response/status code\), JSON, DB table relationships.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Week 2: React basics \(components/state/forms\) and reading existing UI components.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Week 3: API route basics + Prisma queries + auth checks.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Week 4: deliver one small full feature end-to-end \(example: room description\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Practice rule: always explain the feature in plain English before coding.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(12\) Quick glossary) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Frontend: what users see.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Backend: server logic and rules.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(API: doorway between frontend and backend.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(ORM: library that translates code to DB queries.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Session: logged-in state.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Migration/schema change: database structure update.) Tj
